{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e","id":435085,"title":"Lodges in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-09T19:17:11-07:00","id":435085,"title":"Lodges in 2e","content":"First of all, I absolutely love the Second Edition version of Forsaken, in particular I like how the Harmony rules are built around trying to keep a balance between the Uratha's dual natures.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm not sure what to think about Lodges. Honestly, this is the weakest section of the book and I'm really torn with how to handle them in the game I'm putting together. Anyone have any suggestions or thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2770-forsakensteve","name":"ForsakenSteve","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:31:31-07:00","id":435134,"title":"","content":"have you checked out lodges the pure or lodges the splintered? Both books from forsaken 1e. I'm not sure if the blurb in the beginning after the tribes is all there is concerning them, but those two books go into detail on the activities of each lodge. This also includes requirements to join them (stat wise). <br /> <br /> Think of them as mini close-nit tribes. Or particularly inclusive brotherhoods. Sometimes they are more, sometimes less. The lodge of the lake is a bale hound lodge (not that they know it) worshiping the maeljin of pride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:36:31-07:00","id":435138,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'm very familiar with the 1e Lodges and went through most of them to see which ones would fit in 2e from a mechanics standpoint without any major hacking of the rules involved. I curious if Lodges are intended to have similar benefits in the new edition, such as making additional Gifts favored or bonuses to certain rolls. The Lodges section makes no mention of these kinds of benefits, leading me to think that they are more like clubs with specific interests or purposes, but no mechanical advantages to membership.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2770-forsakensteve","name":"ForsakenSteve","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:43:15-07:00","id":435146,"title":"","content":"I think they have their bonuses, but the word count of 2e denied them that space. Same thing for the... covens? of vampire the requiem. Right after clans there's a similar section with no indepth coverage of them, yet they have full books to them. And I believe Stew has said that anything not obviously changed in 2e core is still in from the first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:47:01-07:00","id":435150,"title":"","content":"Actually, Bloodlines in Requiem did get a bit more &quot;meat&quot; if you will. It mentions what benefits there are to Bloodlines and it generally is consistent with 1e Requiem (a unique disicpline or devotions, additional Bane). Forsaken gives a bit of settings, but little discussion on how to incorporate them into the game. I certainly buy the word count issue, but now I'm trying to figure out what I should do with players who are very likely going to want to be in Lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2770-forsakensteve","name":"ForsakenSteve","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:01:48-07:00","id":435161,"title":"","content":"Find the lodge they want and see how well it works. A lot of them should not require to much of a shift from the former. This includes the apocalypse tribes as lodges, since that was mostly just stat requirements and less bonuses. Naturally gifts and rituals need some tweaking. Things to consider: <br /> <br /> Gifts have facets now, and each facet has the power of a 3 dot gift from 1e. Have a particular gift you liked? Think of the benefits each renown type had from the gift and write up a little split.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:28:42-07:00","id":435203,"title":"","content":"The way 2ed treats Lodges in the corebook is a sort of a cross between Tribe &amp; pack, which makes sense. A more powerful totem than a pack, but less than a Tribe. Ditto for their diffuse location; they are spread out further than a pack but not as much as a Tribe. More involved than a Firstborn, but not as much as a pack totem, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually, I could see some Lodges trying to become Tribes. Unless backed by the players, they'd fail but it is an interesting idea...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:38:40-07:00","id":435210,"title":"","content":"Isn't that the premise of more then a few ghost wolf lodges? Only a few lodges have totems powerful enough to do that though. Which lodge was scarred bear a part of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:41:49-07:00","id":435213,"title":"","content":"It would not surprise me. Though the idea was to increase the totem's power through the actions of it's members","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:18:36-07:00","id":435490,"title":"","content":"I have other problem with 2ed Lodges - they feel... too much specialized? Roman Rite are Catholic priests, all from Storm Lords. 100 Days are werewolves in the Ghana. Those are cool concepts, but comparing them to the Bloodlines and Legacies, they feel to centered on one thing. They sound more as particular Uratha mission, than a faction in Forsaken world. They do not get any reliable mechanics benefits, they have only &quot;one thing&quot; of theirs. I gladly add the <b>Apocalypse</b>'s Tribes as <b>WtF</b> Lodges, as those groups have some history, and some broader ideas to use, even if regional in nature.<br /> <br /> If at least Lodges would give Gifts, or better, some minor special power ( but <b>not</b> the bonuses they have in 1ed, <i>real</i> powers ) they would be more feel as factions, not &quot;dedicated missions&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T03:38:46-07:00","id":435518,"title":"","content":"We've done some brainstorming on how 2e Lodges will work in more detail since the drafts went in. Once I've got some other things off my plate, I'll ask Stew if I can maybe put some of the rewritten sample Lodges I did up for people to take a look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:07:59-07:00","id":435574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=435518#post435518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've done some brainstorming on how 2e Lodges will work in more detail since the drafts went in. Once I've got some other things off my plate, I'll ask Stew if I can maybe put some of the rewritten sample Lodges I did up for people to take a look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean besides the wonderful Lodge of the Field? Because that was great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:21:41-07:00","id":435586,"title":"","content":"Historically Lodges have been pretty freeform as far as membership requirements and benefits go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:39:40-07:00","id":435622,"title":"","content":"OK, so brief question: was the authors' intent that Lodges be <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">tighter-associated groups than Tribes, filling a space between Tribe and Pack, without mechanical aspects? Or are mechanical benefits for Lodges part of the design but simply didn't make it into the book for one reason or another? Trying to nail this down for a club NWoD 2nd Ed chronicle that starts in June, and I want to make sure that we're hewing to the design philosophy of Forsaken 2nd Ed in how we handle Lodges.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1731-jessilaurn","name":"Jessilaurn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:52:11-07:00","id":435634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jessilaurn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=435622#post435622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so brief question: was the authors' intent that Lodges be <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">tighter-associated groups than Tribes, filling a space between Tribe and Pack, without mechanical aspects? Or are mechanical benefits for Lodges part of the design but simply didn't make it into the book for one reason or another? Trying to nail this down for a club NWoD 2nd Ed chronicle that starts in June, and I want to make sure that we're hewing to the design philosophy of Forsaken 2nd Ed in how we handle Lodges.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Lodge of the Field has some mechanical benefits associated with it in the Field of Dogs Hunting Ground, but that is the only example we have of such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:01:15-07:00","id":435638,"title":"","content":"Yes, Lodges have mechanical benefits, like 2e Bloodlines. Like 2e Bloodlines there wasn't the space in the core book to go into Lodge mechanics.<br /> <br /> I don't want to go too into detail about the proposed 2e Lodge structure because it's just that - proposed - rather than finalised in an actual product, but Lodges offer benefits due to both the spiritual bond with the totem and the social organisation of the Lodge members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:09:39-07:00","id":435646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=435210#post435210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that the premise of more then a few ghost wolf lodges? Only a few lodges have totems powerful enough to do that though. Which lodge was scarred bear a part of?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't know about a lot of lodges, two of the lodges from forsaken 2d ed have that goal though.<br /> <br /> According to the rage, which admittedly is first edition, forming a new tribe doesn't actually have anything to do with lodges: you find some ghost wolves willing to join up, and then find a potential totem and convince it to adopt you as a new tribe. <br /> <br /> It had three example new tribes, by the by, secret police/who watches the watcher types who police the forsaken for law breaking, ambassadors who prefer to fight with words before fighting with claws, and gnostic scholars.<br /> <br /> It may be a complete coincidence, but those three potential tribes I could see being the result of a massive influx of former pure converts. The fire touched becoming gnostics, Ivory claws becoming wordsmith negotiators, and predator kings becoming fanatical followers of the forsaken law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:14:41-07:00","id":435981,"title":"","content":"I would dig if Lodges worked like Mystery Cult Initiation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:18:22-07:00","id":436035,"title":"","content":"I think they're meant to be similar to cults, but have more to them, since a werewolf can deal with the spiritual heart of things and pledge their spirit-half to them.<br /> <br /> One thing first edition, I think, left out was the military. I like the Lodge of the Shield, and I think military bases, especially those that harbor military vehicles, would be places Uratha would want to lock down or keep an eye on. It seems like tanks and jets would probably fetch a lot of essence while in use, and many wouldn't go into dormancy so easily when put away. Or if they did, could still be awakened, leaving you with a war machine spirit that thirsts for fire and death that could possibly possess its material reflection or a nearby soldier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:25:02-07:00","id":436046,"title":"","content":"A soldier comes home from the war. He's still a little shaken by his tank being taken out, but he survived the experience. Unfortunately for him the spirit of the tank survived the experience too, and it followed him back.<br /> <br /> Left to its own devices it would be more than happy to keep on riding him, machine operating the operator, until finally they became one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:33:15-07:00","id":436053,"title":"","content":"This is why the Storm Lords hunt the Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:39:26-07:00","id":436056,"title":"","content":"I look forward to more words regarding the Lodges. Right now I've got a whole load of ideas for stuff that could work either as Wererwolf lodges or (yes, I play other RPGs, so shoot me) Space Marine Chapters. I haven't yet decided on how to use these ideas that can go either way, but I'll probably make them ready to unleash when we get the rules for making lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T07:16:47-07:00","id":438366,"title":"","content":"Selling point for me would be to make a decent make-your-own lodges creation system.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:21:27-07:00","id":438653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=438366#post438366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Selling point for me would be to make a decent make-your-own lodges creation system.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This would be awesome, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:34:41-07:00","id":438673,"title":"","content":"The Lodges system I've proposed to Stew would make it very <i>straightforward</i> to create your own Lodge, albeit not quick - the discussed notions for Lodges have a lot more mechanical and social meat to them than previous. Things would certainly be more standardised than the 1e Lodges which tended to be a bit all over the place in terms of their mechanical variety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T10:49:55-07:00","id":438683,"title":"","content":"do they still have requirements stat wise to join? For example: Lodges previously have required cunning: x dots or wisdom x dots. Does that still apply? Is it safe to assume that the lodges in faithful, splintered and other books still exist as they are or are we looking at a fundamental change to them? My brother was particularly fond of the hunter in darkness lodge that was dedicated to finding missing children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T17:13:57-07:00","id":439060,"title":"","content":"I can't wait to get those rules man. Can't you post some example lodges?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T17:49:51-07:00","id":439148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=438683#post438683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do they still have requirements stat wise to join? For example: Lodges previously have required cunning: x dots or wisdom x dots. Does that still apply? Is it safe to assume that the lodges in faithful, splintered and other books still exist as they are or are we looking at a fundamental change to them? My brother was particularly fond of the hunter in darkness lodge that was dedicated to finding missing children.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally of the opinion that far too many of the 1e Lodges had essentially arbitrary joining requirements that had no real equivalent inside the narrative, purely as mechanical 'you must be this tall to ride' limitations. I'm not really a fan of such things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=439060#post439060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't wait to get those rules man. Can't you post some example lodges?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>If</i> Stew decides that the proposed Lodge structure will be what is used, and <i>if</i> Stew's ok with it, then at some point in the future there may be example Lodges posted. Really, though the main problem for me isn't writing Lodges (whether entirely new ones or updating 1e ones) but rather <i>stopping</i> writing them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I find it quite fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T18:21:39-07:00","id":439182,"title":"","content":"That's a fair point, glad to hear it. seems all the newer editions of the world of darkness lines favor creativity and less restrictions. Case in point the entire story teller section about fathers form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T15:18:25-07:00","id":459426,"title":"","content":"Since their is a 2ed lodge thread I might as well use it. <br /> <br /> Okay, so my friends and I started playing our 2ed game in hunting grounds Tokyo. We finished it and want to start another game in the same setting. One of my friends wants his character to be in a samurai lodge. I don't know any in Forsaken but I do know one from Apocalypse. So I present him with the Hakken and he likes it. We try to translated to Forsaken 2ed but the problem was we didn't know how since the description for lodges was pretty vague and not much information. So my question is: are the rules for lodges still the same?<br /> <br /> So far we decided the lodge to be from:<br /> Eldoth or Storm Lord <br /> Signature gift: Weather or Evasion <br /> (1ed) Prerequisite: Honor #? Weaponry (katana)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T16:16:02-07:00","id":459473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=459426#post459426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since their is a 2ed lodge thread I might as well use it.<br /> <br /> Okay, so my friends and I started playing our 2ed game in hunting grounds Tokyo. We finished it and want to start another game in the same setting. One of my friends wants his character to be in a samurai lodge. I don't know any in Forsaken but I do know one from Apocalypse. So I present him with the Hakken and he likes it. We try to translated to Forsaken 2ed but the problem was we didn't know how since the description for lodges was pretty vague and not much information. So my question is: are the rules for lodges still the same?<br /> <br /> So far we decided the lodge to be from:<br /> Eldoth or Storm Lord<br /> Signature gift: Weather or Evasion<br /> (1ed) Prerequisite: Honor #? Weaponry (katana)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not assume that the rules for lodges will still be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T22:06:32-07:00","id":459677,"title":"","content":"Id just make the lodge and worry about the rules later. <br /> <br /> Anyone else notice lodge of the shield is now an iron master lodge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T22:25:54-07:00","id":459682,"title":"","content":"Game's incomplete to me without the lodge structures. I used to make whole character concepts out of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T23:07:39-07:00","id":459696,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, but it's not like 1st ed lodges were readily consistent. It is easy enough to replicate them though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T04:56:58-07:00","id":459816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=459682#post459682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game's incomplete to me without the lodge structures. I used to make whole character concepts out of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>suspect </i>- and this is not an official promise or anything, nor a concrete prediction, I'm just a writer and Stew is the decision-maker who I am explicitly <i>not</i> speaking for - that once the final book has been made available with corrections and errata folded in, we may see some sample Lodges down the line on the blog, and these will reveal whatever new structure the 2e Lodge system takes.<br /> <br /> I know that if Stew slipped me off the leash I'd be happily updating old Lodges to 2e at a pretty much constant rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T12:50:48-07:00","id":460323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=459816#post459816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that if Stew slipped me off the leash I'd be happily updating old Lodges to 2e at a pretty much constant rate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which is good, because you're good at it, but hey, leave a little room for someone else maybe, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:14:21-07:00","id":460361,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to see what happens with new Lodges. They've stopped most vampire bloodlines from offering disciplines. But that was never really an issue with Lodges, most of whom didn't have any gifts unique to them, mostly just having a fetish or rite.<br /> <br /> With all non-Moon gifts being available now to everyone, outside of Auspice-oriented lodges I don't think we'd see more Shadow Gifts from lodges. But I guess it would be possible to have certain Shadow gifts that are just cheaper for Lodge members than 'ordinary' Uratha.<br /> <br /> I've said before I liked the idea of lodges offering specific sacred prey, and it looks like it's popped up in some of the example ones but isn't going to be the defining factor of a lodge.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is, I hope it's different from before and I'm sure it'll be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:21:26-07:00","id":460365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=460323#post460323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is good, because you're good at it, but hey, leave a little room for someone else maybe, eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Meet me in the Onyx Path fighting pit and we'll settle this the freelancer way! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2e Lodges, made with Genuine Blood, Sweat &amp; Tears!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=460361#post460361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all non-Moon gifts being available now to everyone, outside of Auspice-oriented lodges I don't think we'd see more Shadow Gifts from lodges. But I guess it would be possible to have certain Shadow gifts that are just cheaper for Lodge members than 'ordinary' Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this thing where I hate XP discounts of any kind on Lodges. Among other things they provide perverse incentives around character building - don't be good at the thing this Lodge is supposed to be good at, because that way you'll be better off XP-wise by buying it cheaper once you're in; you can avoid this by refunding Experiences to a character who's already invested, of course, but that feels rather odd. It's also a kinda dull benefit, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:27:49-07:00","id":460371,"title":"","content":"I guess if you really start publishing Lodges in a blog post I would like to see the ones mentioned in the corebook first for completion sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:31:40-07:00","id":460376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=460365#post460365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this thing where I hate XP discounts of any kind on Lodges. Among other things they provide perverse incentives around character building - don't be good at the thing this Lodge is supposed to be good at, because that way you'll be better off XP-wise by buying it cheaper once you're in; you can avoid this by refunding Experiences to a character who's already invested, of course, but that feels rather odd. It's also a kinda dull benefit, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Custom merits, like the ones afforded by Mystery Cult Initiation are cool. After all, aren't Lodges sorta like cults to begin with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:38:09-07:00","id":460378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=460365#post460365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this thing where I hate XP discounts of any kind on Lodges. Among other things they provide perverse incentives around character building - don't be good at the thing this Lodge is supposed to be good at, because that way you'll be better off XP-wise by buying it cheaper once you're in; you can avoid this by refunding Experiences to a character who's already invested, of course, but that feels rather odd. It's also a kinda dull benefit, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't exactly being a proponent of it but there do seem to be people who want unique shadow gifts. I prefer the shadow gifts to be available to everyone.<br /> <br /> Ideally people will be pleased with whatever comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:48:23-07:00","id":460388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=460378#post460378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't exactly being a proponent of it but there do seem to be people who want unique shadow gifts. I prefer the shadow gifts to be available to everyone.<br /> <br /> Ideally people will be pleased with whatever comes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>They will ultimately be open for everyone, it'll just cost considerably less to learn the gift in question to members. Prolly unlock them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T14:50:05-07:00","id":460424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=460365#post460365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e Lodges, made with Genuine Blood, Sweat &amp; Tears!</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoa: Major reveal: 2E Lodges will admit vampires, prometheans, and changelings!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T15:03:20-07:00","id":460431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_c