<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:27:02-07:00","id":466307,"title":"","content":"If the 2ed Lodges mechanics would be shown in foreseeable future? I have some <b>Apocalypse</b> stuff to talk as porting for <b>Forsaken</b>, and Lodges would be best to do this...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:29:48-07:00","id":466311,"title":"","content":"They'll show it, when they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:47:35-07:00","id":466324,"title":"","content":"Que Sera, Sera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T12:46:34-07:00","id":466394,"title":"","content":"It's not like they're going to be so mechanically complex anything you do now would be worthless. If you really feel the need to convert some tribes to lodges, just go for it. You can make changes to them whenever lodges are re-introduced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:06:18-07:00","id":466412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=466307#post466307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the 2ed Lodges mechanics would be shown in foreseeable future? I have some <b>Apocalypse</b> stuff to talk as porting for <b>Forsaken</b>, and Lodges would be best to do this...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a couple on my mind that I want to work on, especially from Apocalypse to Forsaken. I'm planning on making a Mage lodge, kind of like how the Tremere went from Mages to Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:31:41-07:00","id":466447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=466394#post466394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like they're going to be so mechanically complex anything you do now would be worthless. If you really feel the need to convert some tribes to lodges, just go for it. You can make changes to them whenever lodges are re-introduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not need them for now run game, maybe for continuation on the end of year. But mechanics of Lodges, especially benefits others than &quot;New dots are cheaper&quot; would be god send for those that would like to work with setting, in expanding it. If I want to tweak some Lodges, purely on mechanics principles, and then my mechanics would be not coherent with 2ed general line - my hobbyst work go to waste, when I need to rewrite mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, does not the month after the release of corebook enough time to make general mechanics for Z-Splat? Does not we see 2ed Bloodlines on webpage about one month after <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:37:17-07:00","id":466453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=466447#post466447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does not the month after the release of corebook enough time to make general mechanics for Z-Splat? Does not we see 2ed Bloodlines on webpage about one month after <b>Blood &amp; Smoke</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that I'm not a developer and might be wrong on this, here goes: what timetable <b>Requiem </b>is or was on does not necessarily equate to a similar timetable for <b>Forsaken</b>. Or any other game, for that matter. I wouldn't read too much into that, either way, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T14:17:22-07:00","id":466523,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's entirely within the realm of possibility that they will never post Lodges. So you'll either have to wait, or do it yourself and make adjustments when the time comes.<br /> <br /> I understand the developer, Stew Wilson, is on twitter as DigitalRaven. He would be the one to ask. I also suppose it couldn't hurt to ask Rich Thomas, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-02-2015, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T14:56:55-07:00","id":466549,"title":"","content":"In that case, I will stick to 1ed mechanics and rules for lodges. I have no problem with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T17:44:58-07:00","id":466746,"title":"","content":"I'm ignoring them, mostly because my wife decided to be a cop and lodge of the shield would really explain why a character with her crappy stats as a cop could get on the force. &quot;Connections.&quot; <br /> <br /> As such I'll deal with the rules when they come up (ignore them mostly) and just go with what I'm doing. Future games will use the correct style but not mid game.<br /> <br /> Edit: and especially considering lodge of the shield switched from blood talons to iron masters (which was really pretty logical.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T21:30:49-07:00","id":466991,"title":"","content":"Okay, here is then fan 2ed Lodges question - how to get rid of &quot;New dots are cheapen&quot; Lodges advantages? It felt sooo... cWoD when game came out, not the proper Z-Splat of gamelines. Also, I really hated &quot;when you join the Lodge, you get Fetish&quot; thing - it felt undeserving. You are dedicating your life to the pursuits of Lodge and all you got is the price break and magical item you could get very similar if you are or know Fetish Smith. ( Not that Lodge members would not used Fetishes, but being one of two major advantages to joining? )<br /> <br /> In comparison to the <b>Mage</b> Legacies that added you next Arcana AND giving you really unique powers, it sounds so weak.<br /> <br /> For the advantage, beside opening new Gifts List, I think characters could get third Affinity Renown. With system based on the Gifts Facets opening with Renowns, it does make big advantage and not so bluntly &quot;New dot is cheaper&quot;. The problem is that mostly to the Lodge would join characters with the high Renowns on the start - logical is that the requirements for the Cunning-based Lodge would fulfill the Cunning high character, like Irraka or Iron Master. What would they get from &quot;doubling&quot; their Renown? In Legacies sketch, there is idea that characters with &quot;twice Ruling Arcana&quot; will get price break on instant casting. But Renowns are only used to unlock the Facets - or do they?<br /> <br /> Oh, and what about the Lodges Totem bonus? Maybe all members are treated &quot;as pack&quot; and get Totem Advantages, even if they are spread across the globe? It would be nice, simple, and cool concept. Only on how powerful would be Lodge patron? Rank 3, Rank 4? Or maybe even Rank 5?<br /> <br /> Beside this, Lodge should be more connected to Primal Urge - seeing both Bloodlines 2ed and Legacies 2ed scateches, I would say that character can join Lodge on as low as Primal Urge 2. Certain Renown requirements ( up to twice two dots ) is in order, I so pose, as they mark deeds of character. But beside some rare occasions one skill on max three dots, I would rather point to two Skills at two dots requirement OR certain Merits, not both of those requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T16:39:10-07:00","id":467964,"title":"","content":"There is no such thing as 'affinity renown' in 2E. All renown purchases costs 3xp, and there isn't any &quot;You can't raise X renown because your primary ones are lower&quot; either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:44:40-07:00","id":468090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/435085-lodges-in-2e?p=467964#post467964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such thing as 'affinity renown' in 2E. All renown purchases costs 3xp, and there isn't any &amp;quot;You can't raise X renown because your primary ones are lower&amp;quot; either.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but you do get a greater benefit from raising your Auspice's primary Renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"k